WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
The Covid-19 crisis created
a serious recession worldwide

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.760
and put the European economy on its knees.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.360
Now we need €750 billion
to rebuild our Union,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.400
a new EU that is sustainable,
green, socially inclusive,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.040
digital and doesn't leave
anyone behind.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.480
And there are solutions to find
that kind of money,

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.200
 without making most citizens pay.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.560
Member States leaders
need to take action!

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.920
Today, millions of jobs are at risk

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.800
and the risk is greater than ever
that we lose sight of the climate emergency.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.680
The risk is high that, like after the 2008 crisis,

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.560
billions will be handed to banks

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.480
while the costs of the crisis will be paid by the citizens

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.280
through austerity measures.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.360
We're not going to let that happen.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.680
Europe needs more money for its citizens,

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.160
now more than ever,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.080
to save jobs,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.800
to save SMEs,
to improve our healthcare system,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.440
to insulate houses, to invest in trains
and bike lanes,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:07.080
in cleaner energy and farming,
which can create millions of green jobs,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.240
by stimulating the flow of revenues to the EU.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.200
Own resources are basically money that go

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.520
into the European Union budget
without adding further pressure either

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.840
on people or on national budgets,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.240
but rather by pursuing policies

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.880
that no Member State could efficiently

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.240
 implement on its own, 

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.400
such as the protection of the environment

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.800
and the preservation 
of a fair and social Europe.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.720
The key issue is where do we find that money?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.720
We have proposed several options,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.560
have the largest companies in the EU contribute

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.600
and pay their fair share of taxes.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.480
Right now, multinational companies
harboring their gains in fiscal havens

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.680
don't pay any tax on the profit they make.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.120
The average corporate tax rate in Europe

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.920
has fallen by half over the last 40 years.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.080
With a solid corporate tax rate agreed

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.920
at EU level, we could stop the race to the bottom

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.040
and generate the resources necessary

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.680
to face common European challenges.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.600
We have big digital companies like Google and Amazon

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.320
which benefit from loopholes.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.640
But sometimes they pay no taxes at all in Europe.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.400
So, if an agreement is not reached

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.920
at the international level,
Europe should take the lead.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.520
If we tax big digital companies,

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.880
we will have enough money
to finance entirely

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.120
the Next Generation EU.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.240
If we tax the digital companies,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.440
we could supplement the budget
of our union

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.560
 and make our tax system fairer.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.920
We need to reduce the plague

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.240
of tax evasion and tax fraud

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.240
that takes money from the citizens.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.080
But we also need to finally start
taxing financial transactions.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.960
Big financial players need to pay
their fair share to society.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.520
When all of us buy a phone,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.960
we pay a VAT of minimum 15 %.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.240
Even for basic necessities like food,

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.680
even the most vulnerable pay a minimum of 5.5 %.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.560
Why is it that buying stocks 
on financial markets is taxed at 0.0 %?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.520
We call on all Member States to finally create a solid

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.960
financial transaction tax.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.120
It will put a stop to the high frequency trading
bets that lead to

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.160
massive gains for the financial sector,
while threatening our economic stability.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.200
We ask for a Single Market Levy.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.000
See it as a...subscription.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.080
The big companies are the ones
that benefit from us building

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.320
the single market.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.680
And if they use it, they have to pay for it.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.240
That is only fair.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.920
Such a levy, to be proportionally modulated

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.400
according to companies'
turnover would generate billions to be spent on

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.080
our common priorities.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.600
We should use this momentum
to make our economies stronger,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.280
more social and more sustainable.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.080
We need money to make the Green Deal succeed,

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.800
to contribute to creating millions of green jobs

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.320
in all our countries, while preserving

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.360
a habitable planet.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.840
We also need to have the polluters pay!

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.000
We need measures like a plastic tax

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.240
to draw auction revenues of
the EU Emission Trading Scheme

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.400
and a Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.680
To avoid an outburst of unemployment
and poverty and to win the climate battle

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.200
the Socialists and Democrats
have several concrete solutions on the table.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.240
Now, we need the political will of all
European governments

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.400
if we want these proposals to move forward.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.320
It's now or never. We're now defining
the budget for the next seven years.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.080
We cannot miss this opportunity.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.920
Let’s work together!

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.480
We can make our Union socially fairer and greener!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:53.120
We call on European leaders to agree to our proposals.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.320
For Europe's future, for a better future!

